<article class="env-definition" id="08SS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08SS">Definition <span data-tag="08SS">92.18.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $\mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be a homomorphism of sheaves of rings on $\mathcal{C}$. The <em>cotangent complex</em> $L_{\mathcal{B}/\mathcal{A}}$ is the complex of $\mathcal{B}$-modules associated to the simplicial module </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Omega _{\mathcal{P}_\bullet /\mathcal{A}} \otimes _{\mathcal{P}_\bullet , \epsilon } \mathcal{B}  \]
</div>
  <p> where $\epsilon : \mathcal{P}_\bullet \to \mathcal{B}$ is the standard resolution of $\mathcal{B}$ over $\mathcal{A}$. We usually think of $L_{\mathcal{B}/\mathcal{A}}$ as an object of $D(\mathcal{B})$. </p>
</article>